# UI TypeScript Rules

## Components

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, events, browser APIs).
- One component per file; export name matches filename (`kpi-card.tsx` → `KpiCard`).
- Props as `interface XxxProps`; no inline prop types on large components.

## Data fetching

- All financial data via `lib/api-client.ts` → backend REST API.
- Use TanStack Query for server state; Zustand for UI-only state (theme, month filter).
- No `fetch` to Plaid or direct DB from UI except Plaid Link SDK.

## Styling

- Tailwind v4 + CSS tokens from `docs/design/design-system.md`.
- Money values: JetBrains Mono + `tabular-nums`.
- **Money display:** use `formatMoney()` — always 2 decimal places.
- **Percentages:** use `formatPercent()` from `lib/money-format.ts` — always 2 decimal places.
- No box shadows; flat surfaces with border/surface contrast.

## Types

- Mirror `docs/design/api-contract.md` in `src/types/api.ts`.
- Parse API responses with Zod at the client boundary when feasible.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — business logic in UI
const netSpend = txs.filter(t => !t.name.includes("PAYMENT")).reduce(...)

// ✅ GOOD — consume backend summary
const { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ["summary", month], queryFn: () => api.getSummary(month) })
```
